From 02e111ff23f0febbcbb02cd3fca5f341776166e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:25:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 31/39] drama: speech requests carry voice references, in
 build_prompt_rows's rows

A request's references ({text, vq_codes}) are lowered and refused in the order
and words of the reference's Drama3SpeechPreprocessor. drama_prompt builds the
rows as build_prompt_rows builds them: each part tokenized alone, then one row
per audio frame (<|semantic:0|> plus code 0, then its ten codes). The host
stages those rows' codes through tower.setInput, the decode feedback's
embedding path, so the backbone mixes codebook 1 into audio rows as
embed_backbone does. Requests without a reference build the same prompt and
frames as before.

drama_voice_fixture.json holds the reference's rows and refusals for synthetic
codes (tools/zig/drama_voice_fixture.py); TF_DRAMA3_DIR checks the rows with the
real tokenizer.
